  data:  # 06e9
    kind: invariant  # 06e9
    title: "wolfram.py counts every definition as a call (f[x_] := ... emits calls file -> f), and never analyzes .m files (find_wolfram_files has no caller; *.m not in file_patterns)"  # 06e9
    status: violated  # 06e9
    priority: 2  # 06e9
    parent:  # 06e9
    tags:  # 06e9
    - analysis_quality  # 06e9
    isbefore: []  # 06e9
    duplicate_of: []  # 06e9
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 06e9
    pr_ref:  # 06e9
    description: "Found by the 2026-10-06 docstring audit tail pass; reviewer reproduced both: f[x_]:=..., h[z_]:=..., q[x_]=... each yield a calls edge from the file to f/h/q though nothing calls them; a .m file that classify_dot_m_file labels wolfram produces no symbols. Related, lower severity: every call edge starts at the file node, not the enclosing function (~L284, ~L307), and calls are deduplicated per file and callee name (~L295). wolfram.py's module docstring states all of these."  # 06e9
    fields:  # 06e9
      statement: "A definition is not a call; and a file the analyzer claims (classify_dot_m_file labels it wolfram) is analyzed."  # 06e9
      root_cause: "The left-hand side f[x_] of := / = is itself a call node, and the call walk (~L274-313) does not skip the definition head. file_patterns is ['*.wl','*.wls','*.nb'] (~L333); find_wolfram_files (~L76) would handle .m but nothing calls it and _find_source_files is not overridden."  # 06e9
